{In the next example, we can call in the help of a second passed pawn to stop the enemy king from saving the day.   This position is taken from the 2008 game between Arthur Magafurov
(1959)
and Lev Kuzmichev,  in which Black commits a very instructive mistake.} 36. b6 {[%cal Gb7b6][%csl Ra6]This enables White to turn the tables completely.
36...Kd7
was called for. White can safely resign after
