as the black b-pawn will be the first one to promote.} 37. b5 {[%cal Ra6b5,Ga5a8,Gd5d8][%csl Ga8,Gd8]Make sure you remember this pawn configuration very well. I have seen many games, up to the highest level, in which this surprising pawn break was missed and turned the game upside down.   Creating high tension is a technique that I explain in The Chess Toolbox. It can also be used in endings to create a passed pawn.} axb5 {} 38. a6 {[%cal Ga6a8,Gd5d8][%csl Ga8,Gd8]This was the point. White has just created a second passed pawn. This will soon prove to be too much for the defending king.} b4 {Black also has two passed pawns available, but ours are much more advanced!} 39. d6+ {[%cal Gd6c7,Ga6a8,Gd6d8][%csl Rc7,Ga8,Gd8]39.a7
Kb7
40.d6
is equally strong.} Kxd6 {} 40. a7 {[%cal Ga7a8][%csl Ga8]The pawn is about to promote, which is why Black resigned.} 


