{If we don't have the time or opportunity to bolster our pawn structure to prevent a breakthrough, we will have to rely on our king instead! Make sure your king is always ready to step into the square of the future passed pawn whenever needed. The following position is a good example.   A quick look at this position should tell us that the black pawns are very close to breaking through, and we have to be highly alert and calculate accurately. The conclusion would be that no pawn move can prevent our opponent from queening a pawn, and it is time for our king to step in and level the game:} 1. Ke3 {[%cal Ge3g1,Rf3g2,Rg2g1][%csl Gg1]1.gxf3
is the move that we needed to check. Black wins after the thematic
1...g3
2.hxg3
h3
. It is game over as our f-pawn is standing in the king's way.} fxg2 {} 2. Kf2 {[%cal Gf2g1,Gf2g2][%csl Rg1,Rg2]The king is right on time to stop the pawn from safely queening.} h3 {} 3. Kg1 {[%cal Rg2g1][%csl Gg1,Gc5,Rc7]Neither side can make any progress and the game will end in a draw.} 


