[FEN "8/p4p2/2KP1p1p/7P/3k4/8/2P5/4b3 w - - 0 2"]
[Result "*"]

2. c3+ {This clever move lures one of the two black pieces towards c3 and decides the game.
2.d7
would be too hasty as Black can now stop our pawn with
2...Ba5
and win the game.} Bxc3 {2...Kxc3
3.d7!
would win even quicker.} 3. Kb5 {} a6+ {} 4. Ka4 {This last precise move decides the game as Black is unable to stop our bishop. Bernhardt (1917).} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "009.015"]
[White "Exercise 112 - Pawns vs Bishop"]
[Black "2.1 Pawns against a Piece - Pawns against a Bishop"]
[FEN "8/1p5p/8/PP3p2/5K2/1k5b/8/8 w - - 0 3"]
[Result "*"]

3. Kg3 {The first step we have to take is to prevent the bishop from entering the long diagonal.
3.a6
Bg2!
4.a7
b6
would be an easy win for Black.} Bf1 {} 4. a6 {And then it is time for the breakthrough!} f4+ {4...bxa6
5.b6
is very similar to the main line.} 5. Kf2 {or
5.Kh2} bxa6 {} 6. b6 {The pawn is unstoppable and White wins. Moravec (1913).} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "009.016"]
[White "Exercise 113 - Pawns vs Bishop"]
[Black "2.1 Pawns against a Piece - Pawns against a Bishop"]
