[Result "*"]

1. b4 {First we threaten to push our b-pawn to the other side of the board.} axb3 {1...Bc4
does not really help as the bishop cannot leave the a2-g8 diagonal. White wins after
2.b5
Bxb5
3.f7+
Kxf7
4.Kh7
.} 2. f7+ {And next we are exploiting the fact that the bishop is temporarily unavailable! We queen with check and win after} Kxf7 {} 3. Kh7 {} Bb1+ {} 4. Kh8 {De Feijter (2005).} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "009.020"]
[White "Exercise 117 - Pawns vs Bishop"]
