[Result "*"]

4. Bxg2 {It was impossible to prevent Black from promoting, but luckily we have a stalemate combination at our disposal. First we get rid of the bishop.} hxg2 {} 5. Kh3 {And then we block our pawn and put our king in a tight spot.} g1=Q {Stalemate!
Note that
5...g1=R
leads to the same result and both
5...g1=N+
6.Kg4
Kg6
7.h4
and
5...g1=B
6.Kg4
Be3
7.h4
enable us to trade the last pawn. Segenreich (1973).} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "010.005"]
[White "Exercise 123 - The Bishop Defends"]
