[FEN "8/8/P1p5/8/k1PPb3/3p4/8/2K5 b - - 0 3"]
[Result "*"]

3. Kb3 {This combines attack and defence. We try to mate the king and simultaneously attack the c4-pawn.
3...c5
4.d5!
Kb3
5.Kd2
wins for White.
3...Kb4
4.Kd2
Kxc4
transposes into the main line and is therefore equally strong.} 4. Kd2 {4.a7
Kc3
5.a8=Q
d2+
6.Kd1
Bf3
.} Kxc4 {This was an important pawn because White can no longer create a blockade with ...d4-d5.} 5. a7 {} c5 {And Black wins! This exercise was based on a study, composed by Troitzky in 1914.} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
