[Result "*"]

1. Bxf4 {White had to be very precise to stay on top.
1.Bxh4
gxh2!
and
1.hxg3
f3!
2.gxf3
h3!
would win for Black.} h3 {} 2. Bxg3 {Again, the only move as
2.gxh3
g2
is what Black was aiming at.} hxg2 {} 3. Bf2 {The pawn is under control and White wins. This exercise was inspired by Prokes (1950).} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "010.008"]
[White "Exercise 126 - The Bishop Defends"]
