2.Re6+
Kd5
3.Rd6+
Kc4
4.Rc6+
Kd3
, White can no longer attack our king without spoiling the stalemate.} Kb7 {1...Kd7
2.Rd6+
Ke7
3.Re6+
leads to the same result.} 2. Rc7+ {This time, we can lock up the enemy king in an even smaller area!} Kb8 {} 3. Rc8+ {The easiest, although cutting off the king along the back rank with
3.Rb7+
Kc8
was also perfectly fine.} Ka7 {} 4. Rc7+ {This was an important one as the king can again escape after
4.Ra8+
Kb7
5.Rb8+
Kc6
6.Rc8+
Kd5
7.Rd8+
Kc4
8.Rc8+
Kd3
.} Ka6 {} 5. Ra7+ {} Kxa7 {Stalemate!} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "018.012"]
[White "Exercise 193 - 1...Kc8 or 1...Qb1+?"]
[Black "4.2 The Mighty Queen - Defending with Rook versus Queen"]
