{We will now move on to queen endings with pawns on the board. I have already explained that a direct double attack is rather harmless against a queen, as it would only lead to a piece exchange. Therefore, we must use the skewer and the discovered attack to reach our goal.   In this Introduction, I will present three examples of how we can win the queen, utilising the preparatory techniques of chasing, targeting, and luring.   We finish with a very simple position in which I want to highlight the advantage of the diagonal skewer over the horizontal or vertical one.} 1. -- {} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "019.003"]
[White "1. Chasing"]
[Black "4.3 The Mighty Queen - Winning the Queen"]
