{In this second example, we will use the targeting technique to prepare a discovered attack.   Our aim in this position is to create a battery with our queen as the back piece and one of our pawns as the front piece.} 1. e4+ {[%cal Ge4d5,Rd5e5,Rd5c5][%csl Rd5]We first need to move this pawn out of the way to clear the second rank.} fxe3 {1...Kc5
loses even faster after
2.d4+
Kb6
3.Qb4
, while
1...Ke5
is met by the pretty silent move
2.Qa2!
. We threaten mate with 3.Qd5 and after
2...Kxe4
we can play
3.d3+
and win in a similar fashion to the main line.} 2. Qa2+ {[%cal Ga2d5,Ga2h2,Gd2d4,Gd2d3][%csl Rd5,Rh2]This move sets up the battery with tempo.} Kd4 {} 3. dxe3+ {[%cal Ge3d4,Ga2h2][%csl Rd4,Rh2]The discovered attack decides the game.} Kxe3 {} 4. Qxh2 {} 


