[Result "*"]

{This famous study was composed by Troitzky in 1897. The key is to lure the king towards the centre before we can chase it to a square where it will fall victim to a skewer.} 1. d4+ {[%cal Gd4e5][%csl Re5]This sacrifice does not only pull back the black king. It also creates space for our queen to deliver the right checks.} Kxd4 {Black has nothing better than simply accepting the gift.
1...Kd5
2.Kc3+
Kd6
3.Qa3+
Kd5
is mate after
