5.Qe5
and both
1...Ke4
2.Qc2+
and
1...Kd6
2.Qa3+
Kd5
3.Qc5+
Ke4
4.Qc2+
run into a deadly skewer.} 2. Qf2+ {[%cal Gf2d4,Rd4d5][%csl Rd4]Next, we start pushing the black king back to the seventh rank.
2.Qd2+
Qd3+
3.Qxd3+
Kxd3
4.g6
is another road to victory, but does not teach us anything about targeting and chasing.} Kd5 {Note how every other move runs into a skewer:
2...Ke5
3.Qc5+
Ke4
4.Qc2+
2...Kd3
3.Qc2+
2...Ke4
3.Qc2+
.} 3. Qd2+ {[%cal Gd2d5,Rd5c5][%csl Rd5]} Kc5 {3...Ke5
4.Qc3+
Kd5
4...Kf5
5.Qd3+
5.Qc4+
Kd6
transposes to the main line.} 4. Qb4+ {[%cal Gb4c5,Rc5d5][%csl Rc5]We cannot let the black king escape to b6 !} Kd5 {} 5. Qc4+ {[%cal Gc4d5,Rd5d6][%csl Rd5]We are very close to chasing the black king to a lethal square.} Kd6 {5...Ke5
6.Qc5+
Ke4
7.Qc2+
Ke5
8.Qxh7
also wins for us.} 6. Qd4+ {[%cal Gd4d6,Rd6c7,Rd6e7,Gd4a7,Ga7h7][%csl Rd6,Re7,Rc7,Rh7]This moves combines the chasing and targeting technique to bring both the black king and our queen to the seventh rank with tempo.} Kc7 {} 7. Qa7+ {[%cal Ga7h7][%csl Rh7,Rc7]} Kc8 {} 8. Qxh7 {Mission accomplished !} 


