{The previous two sections gave us a very specific task to either win the queen, or mate the king in a set number of moves. We could use this intel to focus on undefended queens or vulnerable kings and bring only the tools required for that particular purpose.   Now it's time to raise the bar by solving slightly more challenging mix-exercises, where the only information we have is that we need to win the game. As a result, we have to figure out for ourselves whether to reach this goal by either winning the queen or mating the king. And in how many moves. Just like in our games.   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


