{This section taught us three important techniques that we can use to promote our pawns without the
(slow)
assistance of our king. We started with an example in which we could use our rook to support our pawn to the other side of the board. Next, we witnessed how we could thwart the defence by either blocking a file, or by luring away the defending rook.   You can use these, and many more, techniques to solve the exercises.   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


