{This position was reached by Derek Ma
(1961)
and Anthony Boron
(2024)
in Winnipeq in 2018.  Black played well in this game and is ready to push for a win in this ending. However, not after the following move.} 60. e3 {This move looks very tempting, but has a clear drawback.
60...Rb2!
was the way to go, with a winning advantage after
61.Kg1
e3
62.fxe3
Kxg3
.} 61. Rc5 {[%cal Gc5h5][%csl Rf5,Rg5,Rh5]The king can no longer access the fifth rank and is trapped in a mating net! Black resigned because it is mate after the following sequence.} Rb2 {} 62. Rg5 {[%cal Gg5g4][%csl Rg4]} 


