3. Kh1 {In the long run, we cannot really stop the black c-pawn, and our own pawn is not going anywhere either. This is why we opt for Plan B: creating a stalemate in the corner.} c3 {} 4. c8=Q {First we get rid of our pawn.} Rxc8 {} 5. Rg8 {And then our rook!} Rc7 {} 6. Rg7 {Black cannot ignore the rook forever. The draw is inevitable.} Rc6 {} 7. Rg6 {} Rc5 {} 8. Rg5 {} Rc4 {} 9. Rg4 {} Rxg4 {Klefisch (1967).} 


