[White "Conclusion - The Reliable Rook - Catching the bishop"]
[Black "5.7 The Reliable Rook - Catching the Bishop"]
[FEN "rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1"]
[Result "*"]

{This section taught us that defending the bishop against rook ending is quite simple when you can place your king in the right corner; the one where your king stands on a different colour than your bishop.   We also learned that locking up the enemy king in the wrong corner and exploiting tactical opportunities are the most important tools we need in this ending as an attacker. Make sure you bring them when you start solving the exercises!   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "031.006"]
[White "Exercise 397 - Catching the bishop"]
