[FEN "5K2/8/P5b1/2p5/8/1k6/8/4N3 w - - 0 2"]
[Result "*"]

2. Nf3 {Our aim is to keep the bishop away from the long diagonal.} Kc3 {This is the best attempt for Black as
2...Be4
is simply met with
3.Nd2+
.} 3. Ng5 {The knight controls the important e4-square which means that Black is unable to prevent our pawn from promoting. Mar (1924).} 


