[Result "*"]

3. Nc4 {The knight heads for the queenside with tempo to assist our pawn.} Nb7 {Our knight was taboo because of
3...Nxc4
4.b7
.} 4. Nxd6 {This sacrifice lures the knight to d6.} Nxd6 {4...Nd8
5.b7
Nxb7
6.Nxb7
Kxg6
7.Nxc5
also wins for White.} 5. e5+ {We apply the luring technique for the second time! This double attack leaves the black king no other option but to capture our pawn.} Kxe5 {5...Kxg6
6.exd6
.} 6. g7 {The pawn promotes and White wins.
6.b7
is equally strong. (V.Platov & M.Platov 1914).} 


