{I hope you enjoyed the second part of this book and feel ready for Test 2! It consists of 36 exercises, with an equal amount of attacking and defensive positions. The aim is to assess whether you master the tools that we have practiced in this
(and the previous!)
part. This should be the case if you can solve at least 75% of the exercises correctly.   There is no need to worry if you don't pass this bar in one go. In that case, you can simply review the critical topics once more and retry the test later.   Flash Cards  Before we start the test, you can review the summarizing flash cards first. They can serve as a reminder of the most important techniques that we came across in this part.   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


[Event "1001 Chess Endgame Exercises for Club Players"]
[Round "039.002"]
