{This section showed us that we can defend ourselves against the dangerous rook and bishop combination by creating an evacuation square for our king, by identifying and protecting our weakest spot, and by creating a counterattack on one of our opponent's pieces.   Exercises:   It is now time to improve our defensive skills by solving exercises where we are on the defending side. We start with positions in which we must defend to survive, focusing completely on parrying the threat and being content with a draw as the final outcome of the game.   In the remaining exercises, we have to be more ambitious and find the narrow path to victory!   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


