Qa8
3.Rb8
Qxb8
4.Bf4+
1...Qxb4
2.Bf8+
1...Qa8
2.Rb8
Qa7
3.Be3
Qxb8
4.Bf4+
.} 2. Rb8 {And again! We really want the black king and queen on the same diagonal.} Qc6 {2...Qxb8
3.Bf4+
2...Qc5
3.Bf8+
.} 3. Rb6 {} Qxb6 {} 4. c5+ {And here we go. This move lures the two black pieces to the same diagonal, after which we can decide the game with a skewer.} Qxc5 {4...Kxc5
5.Be3+
.} 5. Bf8+ {} Kc6 {} 6. Bxc5 {} Kxc5 {} 7. h5 {The white pawn queens first and White wins. Sehwers (1903).} 


