[White "Conclusion - Two Major Pieces - Two Rooks"]
[Black "10.2 Two Major Pieces - Two Rooks"]
[FEN "rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1"]
[Result "*"]

{This section featured three different examples in which we could coordinate our rooks to win a rook, promote our pawn, or mate the king. It was often important to pick the right rook for an attack on the king to prevent it from running away.   Exercises   It is now time to sharpen your rook skills. I have created a set of exercises in which the assignment is to win the game, without any prior knowledge of how to reach this goal. Just like in your own games.   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


