{In this section, you’ll face a series of exercises where the goal is to defend against the dangerous rook and knight duo.  Defence is never easy, but you can rely on the skills that you have developed in earlier chapters. When approaching each position, begin by identifying your opponent’s threats. Remember that understanding their plan is the first step to stopping it!   Then, choose the appropriate defensive techniques to safeguard your king or pieces. To refresh your memory, here are the most important defensive techniques we have encountered so far:  - Parrying the threat    - Picking the right square for your king or piece   - Creating an evacuation square for your king     - Protecting your weakest spot    - The counterattack    - Defending with a tactical combination   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


