{In this section, we explored two examples where a rook and a knight successfully outplayed an opposing queen.   The first was a composed study, in which the enemy king and queen had considerable manoeuvring space in the centre. However, we managed to restrict their activity by positioning our rook close to the enemy pieces, supported by tactical motifs.   Additionally, I presented an example from a real game to demonstrate how such scenarios can also arise in practical play. Even in your own games, accidents can occur when facing a well-coordinated rook and knight.   Exercises  The most effective way to sharpen your rook and knight skills is by solving targeted exercises. I’ve prepared plenty for you and I hope you enjoy working through them.   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


