{Congratulations! You have arrived at the final test!   This test consists of 77 exercises. In 48 of them, your task is to decide the game by either mating the king, winning material, or promoting a pawn. The remaining 29 exercises focus on defending your king and pieces, helping you sharpen your defensive skills.   The aim of the test   The goal is to assess whether you can apply the attacking and defensive techniques you’ve learned in your own games. If you manage to solve at least 57 out of 77 exercises correctly
(approximately 75%)
, you can be very proud of yourself. It means you’re ready to take your calculation skills to an even higher level.   If you don’t reach that mark just yet, no worries. You can be proud as well because you came this far. I recommend you to identify the areas that need improvement, revisit those sections with care, and try the test again when you’re ready.   Good luck!} 1. -- {} 


